014 the market hasn't caught on yet.\nLive scenario. Iran conflict / Strait-of-Hormuz risk \u2014 crude+gas+metals+chemicals+defense rally in PARALLEL; airlines/autos/paints hit \u2014 the cascade favours Upstream E&P (crude/gas producers), Defense and pressures Refiner & OMC, Paints. Parallel cross-currents: safe-haven bid, Hormuz freight and supply fear push Defense, Shipping, Metals and Specialty Chemicals UP \u2014 even as the demand-shock side pressures Refiners and Airlines. This is NOT a one-way oil trade.\nLive scenario. India major gas discovery (Andaman basin) \u2014 energy-independence re-rate \u2014 the cascade favours Upstream E&P (crude/gas producers), EPC & Infrastructure and pressures \u2014. A domestic gas discovery re-rates the gas value chain (city-gas, pipelines, upstream) and eases the import bill (rupee-supportive) \u2014 a structural slow-burn re-rating, not a shock.\nFirm layer. Sector calls aren't destiny \u2014 a wide-moat, dominant name (think IndiGo in Airlines) can rise even when its sector cascade says short. Ask me about any ticker to test that.\nNet. Stay patient and structural: anchor on the under-priced structural theses, trade the live cascades as spreads, and let firm moats veto the sector where they earn it."}